FUN_000789-T1	eggNOG-mapper	CDS	1	336	563.0	+	.	ID=FUN_000789-T1;em_target=1041607.K0K7J8;em_score=563.0;em_evalue=1.27e-201;em_tcov=100.0;em_searcher=diamond;em_OGs=KOG1649@1|root,KOG1649@2759|Eukaryota,38F3D@33154|Opisthokonta,3NX1J@4751|Fungi,3QP1P@4890|Ascomycota,3RS6I@4891|Saccharomycetes;em_COG_cat=K;em_desc=Part of the chromatin structure-remodeling complex (RSC) which is involved in transcription regulation and nucleosome positioning. RSC is responsible for the transfer of a histone octamer from a nucleosome core particle to naked DNA. The reaction requires ATP and involves an activated RSC-nucleosome intermediate. Remodeling reaction also involves DNA translocation, DNA twist and conformational change. As a reconfigurer of centromeric and flanking nucleosomes, RSC complex is required both for proper kinetochore function in chromosome segregation and, via a PKC1-dependent signaling pathway, for organization of the cellular cytoskeleton. This subunit is essential for mitotic growth and required for cell cycle progression (By similarity);em_max_annot_lvl=4751|Fungi;em_PFAMs=GATA,SNF5;em_Preferred_name=SFH1;em_KEGG_ko=ko:K11770;em_BRITE=ko00000,ko03021,ko03036;em_GOs=GO:0000228,GO:0000785,GO:0000790,GO:0003674,GO:0003676,GO:0003677,GO:0005488,GO:0005575,GO:0005622,GO:0005623,GO:0005634,GO:0005694,GO:0006139,GO:0006259,GO:0006275,GO:0006281,GO:0006302,GO:0006325,GO:0006333,GO:0006337,GO:0006338,GO:0006351,GO:0006354,GO:0006355,GO:0006357,GO:0006366,GO:0006368,GO:0006725,GO:0006807,GO:0006950,GO:0006974,GO:0006996,GO:0007059,GO:0008150,GO:0008152,GO:0009058,GO:0009059,GO:0009889,GO:0009987,GO:0010467,GO:0010468,GO:0010556,GO:0010564,GO:0016043,GO:0016070,GO:0016586,GO:0018130,GO:0019219,GO:0019222,GO:0019438,GO:0022411,GO:0031055,GO:0031323,GO:0031326,GO:0031498,GO:0031974,GO:0031981,GO:0032774,GO:0032984,GO:0032986,GO:0032991,GO:0033262,GO:0033554,GO:0034641,GO:0034645,GO:0034654,GO:0034728,GO:0043044,GO:0043170,GO:0043226,GO:0043227,GO:0043228,GO:0043229,GO:004